<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Working by transfinite induction, we may reduce to the case where $B$ is obtained from $A$ by adjoining a single non-degenerate simplex, and therefore to the universal case $B = \Delta ^ n$, $A = \bd \Delta ^ n$. Now the inclusion in question is isomorphic to $\Lambda ^{n+2}_{1} \subseteq \Delta ^{n+2}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>